2. Components in the container images
-------------------------------------

deploy/Dockerfile builds the targets runtime, product, agents, opencode, ops
and acceptance (test-only).

Base images
  python:3.12-slim-bookworm   CPython (PSF-2.0) on Debian 12 "bookworm". Each
                              Debian package keeps its own licence, recorded in
                              the image under /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright.
  node:22-bookworm-slim       Only Node.js (MIT, with the third-party licences
                              listed in Node's own LICENSE) and its bundled npm
                              (Artistic-2.0) are copied into the images.

Debian packages installed by the Dockerfile
  git                         GPL-2.0-only (git's COPYING). Debian's copyright
                              file in the image lists the licences of the
                              parts git includes.
  ca-certificates             MPL-2.0 for the certificate data and
                              GPL-2.0-or-later for the Debian packaging and
                              scripts (Debian's copyright file, bookworm
                              version 20230311+deb12u1)

Source of the Debian packages
  The corresponding source of every Debian package in the images, including the
  packages of the python:3.12-slim-bookworm base, is in Debian's source archive.
  For the version installed in a given image (`dpkg-query -W` inside it), the
  source is at https://sources.debian.org/src/<source-package>/<version>/ and,
  for every version Debian has published, at
  https://snapshot.debian.org/package/<source-package>/<version>/.
  deploy/Dockerfile installs git and ca-certificates from Debian 12 "bookworm"
  at build time and does not pin their versions. On 2026-10-04 bookworm carries:
    git 1:2.39.5-0+deb12u3
      https://sources.debian.org/src/git/1:2.39.5-0+deb12u3/
      https://snapshot.debian.org/package/git/1%3A2.39.5-0%2Bdeb12u3/
    ca-certificates 20230311+deb12u1
      https://sources.debian.org/src/ca-certificates/20230311+deb12u1/
      https://snapshot.debian.org/package/ca-certificates/20230311%2Bdeb12u1/
  An image built on another date may carry another bookworm version; its
  `dpkg-query -W` output names it.

